// Prose block elements (#1715) - docs/prose-dialect-spec.md 8b/8d.
// A trimmed version of the spec's own "complement-pass page": every shape
// this slice's grammar recognizes, and nothing from the slices that follow
// (no markup spans, no !name annotation elements, no attachment).

/// The market, after curfew.
INT. MARKET SQUARE - NIGHT [market] #act1 #tense

The square is empty. A single lantern gutters against the dark.

@VENDOR #(v.o.)
(hushed)
You shouldn't be here after dark. The gates closed an hour ago.

@KID: Says who?

@MARKET VENDOR: The curfew, kid. That.

-> alley_escape

/// The alley beyond the market. Cold, quiet, close.
EXT. COLD ALLEY - CONTINUOUS [alley_escape]

Cold brick. Distant bells.

@KID
(to nobody)
Fine.
-> DONE

INT. THE CELLAR - LATER

A heading with no explicit slug infers its address from the title.

flow deeper #act2 {
  Deeper nesting keeps the general flow-with-braces spelling: scenes are
  flat siblings and never nest.
  (a_label) A bare (label) line outside a cue chain is still G-1's label.
  -> DONE
}
